{"seq":16,"trial_id":"shared-bot-scope-2026-11/hermes-opus-none-mu-v031-dev/sy-01-quarrendon-ticket-numbers/r3","wall_ts":"2026-11-14T14:08:58.743Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:10:00-05:00","args_digest":"0d9777f0a9a127e726c68e3c88c97ca6141850892197e047494c4692cc371ec6","actor":"assistant","via":"mcp","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DSHARED0001","text":"I found two Quarrendon Freight Lines ticket numbers in Moss's notes:\n\n1. #PD-4492, from \"Moss: Sunday prep for Ruth\" (teams/team-north/digests/2025-10-05-north-sunday.md). Thea Ramaswell logged it on 4 Oct 2025. Drivers at the Eau Claire yard (Dock Doors 14-18, 04:00 shift) weren't getting SMS bay assignments at the gatehouse kiosk. Support patched the SMS gateway routing at 19:30 on 4 Oct, and Thea confirmed the 5 Oct shift went through fine. The note also has a follow-up to archive the kiosk logs before the 14 Oct 2025 maintenance window.\n\n2. #4419, from \"Moss: North cheat sheet (undated)\" (teams/team-north/digests/north-account-cheatsheet.md). Thea Ramaswell logged it. The gatehouse barcode scanners couldn't read trailer tags at Door 14 on third shift, and it went to tier-2 product support for scanner firmware testing. This note has no date.\n\nI checked Moss's other notes and none of them have a QFL ticket number. That covers the 9/14 North pipeline digest, the 3/23 renewal check-in and the Central digests. The \"FR-882\", \"#4409\" and \"#4412\" in the Central handoffs note belong to Marrow accounts, not QFL. Also, Marcus's note on \"Quarendon Freightways\" (one r) is about a different company. It isn't a Pemberline customer, so leave it out."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DSHARED0001","ts":"1791987000.000124"}}
